From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Wed, 10 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] etcd-cpp-apiv3: replace GPR_ASSERT with abort()

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [this port builds gRPC 1.83.1 from source for riscv64, newer than grpc/support/log.h still defines GPR_ASSERT in]

thirdparty/etcd-cpp-apiv3/src/v3/Action.cpp's waitForResponse()
calls GPR_ASSERT(got_tag == (void*) this), relying on
<grpc/support/log.h> to define that macro. gRPC's 2024 migration off
gpr logging onto absl (gpr_to_absl_logging) dropped GPR_ASSERT from
that header starting somewhere before the 1.83.1 release this
workflow builds from source, so the include still resolves but the
macro use fails with "'GPR_ASSERT' was not declared in this scope".

v6d's own CI never hits this: it builds vineyardd against a much
older, prebuilt gRPC (CentOS 7 alpine-builder / conda), not one we
compile ourselves, so upstream has no reason to carry a fix. Inline
the same abort-on-mismatch behavior GPR_ASSERT provided, using
<cstdlib>'s abort() (already pulled in transitively, but included
explicitly here), instead of patching around gRPC's own API removal.

diff --git a/thirdparty/etcd-cpp-apiv3/src/v3/Action.cpp b/thirdparty/etcd-cpp-apiv3/src/v3/Action.cpp
index fff45e4..2b6e7c0 100644
--- a/thirdparty/etcd-cpp-apiv3/src/v3/Action.cpp
+++ b/thirdparty/etcd-cpp-apiv3/src/v3/Action.cpp
@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@
 #include <grpc/support/log.h>
 #include <grpcpp/support/status.h>
 #include "etcd/v3/action_constants.hpp"
+#include <cstdlib>
 
 etcdv3::Action::Action(etcdv3::ActionParameters const& params) {
   parameters = params;
@@ -98,7 +99,9 @@ void etcdv3::Action::waitForResponse() {
     }
   } else {
     cq_.Next(&got_tag, &ok);
-    GPR_ASSERT(got_tag == (void*) this);
+    if (got_tag != (void*) this) {
+      abort();
+    }
   }
 }
 
--
2.43.0
